@@ -72,6 +72,24 @@ EE.on('another-event', emitted, context);
 EE.removeListener('another-event', emitted, context);
 ```
 
+### Subscriptions
+
+`EventEmitter.subscribe` adds a persistent listener like `on` and returns an
+idempotent function that cancels only that subscription:
+
+```js
+var unsubscribe = EE.subscribe('event-name', emitted, context);
+
+unsubscribe();
+unsubscribe(); // No-op.
+```
+
+Unlike `off` (an alias for `removeListener`), the returned cancellation function
+does not match by function or context. It remains tied to its original
+registration, so cancelling it cannot remove another registration made later.
+The listener is still visible through `listeners()` and follows the normal
+registration order until it is cancelled or removed by another API.
+
 ### Tests and benchmarks
 
 To run tests run `npm test`. To run the benchmarks run `npm run benchmark`.
